ffer only in labels, so a symmetric computation should give the same answer. Working it through, cooperating pays 2 and defecting pays 4 if the correlation holds, and cooperating wins once the correlation exceeds 5/7. That seems plausible here, so I'll pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm looking at the twin prisoner's dilemma under A-FDT, where the other copy runs the same algorithm on a different input. I'm checking whether its action depends subjunctively on my node, since A-FDT only intervenes on my node and holds the other's at prior, while the counterfactual-algorithm test suggests the decision function is identical and the inputs differ only in irrelevant details.\n\nI'm weighing whether the twin's output really depends on mine: the algorithm is the same and the inputs differ only in labels, so a symmetric computation should give the same answer. Working it through, cooperating pays 2 and defecting pays 4 if the correlation holds, and cooperating wins once the correlation exceeds 5/7. That seems plausible here, so I'll pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9935,"completion_tokens":733,"total_tokens":10668,"cost":0.0544,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.0544,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03974,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01466},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":390,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}